
========================================================================
  THE DROWNED TOWER
  Fort on the Lake: the island and the first cellars
========================================================================
Seed: 1

== The Fort Docks ==
(The Fort, noon)

The Fort docks. Captain Maren coils a wet rope and does not smile.

MAREN: Row to the Isle of Old Stone. Find out who lands there, and what
moves in the water.

One boat. One hero. Maren waits to hear who goes.

Who rows to the Isle of Old Stone? [final]
  1. The Fighter
     A sword and 8 hit points. Strong at doors.
  2. The Wizard
     A dagger, 4 hit points, and one Sleep spell.
> 1

You belt on the sword and take the oars.

== The Broken Jetty ==
(The Isle of Old Stone, sunset)

Four hours of oars later, the sun is low and the island is close.

A stone jetty runs out from the south shore. Half of it has fallen into
the lake.

On a mooring post, a rope burn shows pale and fresh: someone else lands
here.

Past the end of the jetty, something large moves under the water, a long
shadow, and is gone.

Role: fighter

Where do you go? [plan]
  1. Walk up to the tower shell
  2. Row back to the Fort
     The delve ends here.
> 1

== The Tower Shell ==
(The Isle of Old Stone)

A round tower, thirty feet across, open to the sky. Its upper floors
fell in long ago and lie as rubble on the ground.

A stair climbs the inside wall to a broken top forty feet up. Crows
watch you from the rim with the calm of tax collectors.

Role: fighter

What do you look at? Looking is free. [plan]
  1. Search the rubble
  2. Climb the stair
  3. Move on
> 1

You shift stones for ten minutes. Under the rubble lies a trapdoor of
black oak.

Its iron ring is furred with rust. It lifts with a groan.

Role: fighter

Where do you go? [plan]
  1. Walk to the keeper's cottage
  2. Go down through the trapdoor
  3. Walk back to the jetty
> 2

== The Cellar Stair ==
(Under the tower)

Under the trapdoor a stone stair goes down twenty feet. The air smells
of old oil and wet stone.

At the bottom stands an oak door, swollen in its frame. It is stuck.

Role: fighter

Listen at the door first? [plan]
  1. Listen at the door
  2. Do not listen
> s
Saved to save_fort.json.

Role: fighter

Listen at the door first? [plan]
  1. Listen at the door
  2. Do not listen
> 1

Scratching. Squeaks. Many small feet.

Role: fighter

The door is stuck. What do you do? [final]
  1. Put your shoulder to the door
> r

